menu "LED Status Indicator"

    config LED_STATUS_INDICATOR_ENABLE
        bool "Enable RGB LED status indicator"
        default y
        help
            Drive the onboard WS2812 RGB LED(s) to reflect device state
            (boot, idle, agent thinking, tool execution, Wi-Fi connectivity,
            errors, and one-shot notifications). Disable if the board has
            no addressable RGB LED wired up.

    config LED_STATUS_GPIO_NUM
        int "LED strip data GPIO"
        depends on LED_STATUS_INDICATOR_ENABLE
        default 48
        help
            GPIO driving the WS2812 data line. Defaults to the pin used by
            the board's single onboard RGB LED (see board_peripherals.yaml
            rmt_tx). N16R8 DevKitC-1 variants commonly wire this to GPIO48
            (older/other variants use GPIO38) — if the physical wiring
            differs, update this value.

    config LED_STATUS_LED_COUNT
        int "Number of LEDs on the strip"
        depends on LED_STATUS_INDICATOR_ENABLE
        default 1
        range 1 64
        help
            Number of WS2812 LEDs chained on LED_STATUS_GPIO_NUM. All LEDs
            are driven in sync with the same color/brightness. The stock
            ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 (and clones) ship with a single onboard LED.

    config LED_STATUS_MAX_BRIGHTNESS
        int "Maximum LED brightness (0-255)"
        depends on LED_STATUS_INDICATOR_ENABLE
        default 60
        range 1 255
        help
            Brightness ceiling applied to every rendered color, to keep
            power draw and glare reasonable. Full WS2812 brightness (255)
            is very bright at close range.

endmenu
